// computation kernel
//
// BLAS SYRK (lower triangle):
//   C := alpha * A * A^T + beta * C
//
// A is N x M (i x k)
// C is N x N (i x j), only lower triangle (j <= i) is updated
//
// Optimizations compared to the original kernel:
//  - Loop order is changed to (i, j, k):
//      * For each C(i,j) we keep the accumulator in a register and
//        traverse all k, so C is loaded/stored only once per element.
//      * Along 'k' we access both A(i,k) and A(j,k) contiguously because
//        'k' is the inner dimension of A's layout.
//  - The reduction dimension 'k' is optionally tiled via into_blocks_dynamic.
//    This creates a blocked view of A without changing its physical layout
//    and lets the compiler optimize inner-block computation.
//  - All iteration is expressed via Noarr traversers, as required.
